Z||000000||DjKid||10-08-2000||04:18 AM||||is NOS explosive?<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||10-08-2000||07:35 AM||||NOS by itself is not explosive.It is a medium used to get more oxygen into an engine so you can add more fuel,and hence(check out the fancy word)get more power.Oxygen by itself does not burn,it supports combustion.  <p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 10-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-08-2000||06:51 PM||||What Hugh said... Nitrous Oxide is an "Oxidizer." As used in a automotive applications it's also cryogenic. It cools the intake charge as well as increases the combustion capacity. Sprayed on you it would easily cause severe frostbite.<P>The gas itself doesn't explode. mixed in the right amount with a fuel it goes boom real good.<P>The danger factor of a NOS system is generally pretty low. You do have to make sure the bottle doen't over heat. Some one posted a link to the forums about what happens to a bottle when it gets too hot. The person in that case was lucky. It only blew the car apart. It could have killed someone. ((As I recall that induhvidual left the bottle heater on.))||||reg||1
Z||000003||DjKid||10-08-2000||06:53 PM||||isn't pure oxygen explosive? or liquid oxygen?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-08-2000||07:02 PM||||I had a hard time convincing my wife that oxygen was not an explosive, flamable element. Dangerous? Yes! A small flame will become a big one when in an atmosphere of high oxygen concentration. I finally just turned on the oxygen to the torch, held a lit stir paddle in front of it and used the oxygen to blow the flame out. When mixed with a fuel, then it becomes a different beast altogether.||||reg||1
